//! Rust type definitions for the Milky protocol, version 1.3.
//!
//! # Provenance
//! Generated by the official Milky code generator (`milkygen`) from the Milky IR published for
//! version 1.3.0, then vendored here verbatim with two deliberate local changes, both marked with
//! a `LOCAL PATCH` comment in the code below:
//!
//! 1. The generated doc comments were translated from Chinese to English, because this workspace
//!    keeps every comment in English (see `AGENTS.md`). The translated text is a faithful
//!    translation of the generator's original wording; no code was touched by that pass.
//! 2. An inbound message segment whose `type` this release does not define is preserved as
//!    [`IncomingSegment::Unknown`] instead of being degraded to a placeholder text segment.
//!    Vendored bindings otherwise silently *drop* information that a newer protocol
//!    implementation sent, which contradicts the adapter's promise to lose nothing on ingest.
//!
//! `rustfmt` is deliberately not applied to this file: it keeps the generator's own layout, so a
//! regenerated file can be diffed against this one ignoring the comment translation and the two
//! patches above. Only lines inside comments and the two patches differ; every other code line is
//! byte-for-byte what the generator emitted.
//!
//! # Typing notes
//! - Enumerations that the IR declares as plain string enums (a member's `sex` or `role`, for
//!   example) are typed as `String` by the generator. That is lossless on the wire and keeps the
//!   binding forward compatible, so it is left as generated.
//! - `Input`/`Output` type aliases exist for every one of the 65 protocol endpoints; the typed
//!   client in [`crate::client`] builds directly on them.

